`cpanm App::karr` on Windows (Strawberry Perl 5.42, App::karr 0.602) never
finishes: the suite is green through t/112 and then stands still.

    t/112-handoff-derived-target.t .............. ok
    (hangs)
    perl.exe t/113-native-index-tracked-under.t
    perl.exe -I.../lib .../bin/karr init --name NoPath

That is the subtest "no git binary on PATH: init still leaves the project's
.gitignore alone": `karr init` started through open3 with `PATH` emptied.
After the child was killed the test itself stayed blocked. Tests after t/113
have never run on Windows. (windows-developer hub, docs/karr-windows.md, B6.)

Not diagnosed. Candidates: an emptied PATH on Windows also removes the
directory the libgit2 DLL's dependencies load from (libssl, libssh2 in
`C:\Strawberry\c\bin`); the test reads the child's pipes to EOF before
`waitpid`; `_run_git`'s select loop (k325).

There is no Windows CI: ci.yml and release-binaries.yml are Linux only, and
neither are Git::Native's or Git::Libgit2's.

Done when:
- the suite runs to the end on Windows with a per-test time limit and every
  failure or hang is named (fixed, or skipped on MSWin32 with the reason);
- a `windows-latest` job in ci.yml keeps it that way -- or the decision not
  to support Windows from source is written down and the install path there
  is the binary.

